    {
      "calls": [
        {
          "ID": "toolu_01Ee6r4F4gG5HoFj9cEVnAfM",
          "Name": "submit_read",
          "Input": {
            "assessments": [
              {
                "facts": [
                  "F79",
                  "F80",
                  "F81",
                  "F89",
                  "F59",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S10:F50"
                ],
                "ref": "N1",
                "statement": "The domestic agenda of the new Prime Minister, three months in office, is largely the Greater Manchester devolution model scaled up to UK level: localised employment support, a northern base for No10, and public control of transport.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F92",
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S20:F91"
                ],
                "ref": "N2",
                "statement": "The UK-Scottish partnership so far rests on offers made from Westminster; the only concrete matching commitment from the Scottish Government is the £10 million for defence colleges, so the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers is the first real test of whether the offer is taken up.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "F14",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40"
                ],
                "ref": "N3",
                "statement": "The UK is tightening pressure on Russian energy revenue and speeding up air-defence deliveries alongside the energy ceasefire it lobbied for, not waiting on it, because the ceasefire only takes effect once a start date is confirmed.",
                "supersedes": ""
              }
            ],
            "statements": [
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F80",
                  "F79"
                ],
                "text": "Behind this week's announcements is a Prime Minister who has been in Downing Street only since July, after leaving Westminster in 2017 to become the first Mayor of Greater Manchester."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F89",
                  "F81",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "F59",
                  "S10:F50"
                ],
                "text": "His record as Mayor shows up across the Stories. He brought buses back under public control in Greater Manchester and now fronts Great British Railways' new Derby headquarters. He built the Live Well model there and now offers Scotland devolved DWP employment support. He has also created a Number 10 North."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N1"
                ],
                "text": "Taken together, the domestic programme looks less like a set of separate initiatives than the Manchester devolution model scaled up to Whitehall."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F92",
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S20:F91"
                ],
                "text": "In Scotland the effort so far runs one way. The offers come from the UK government: work through No10 North and the Scotland Office, and a 'serious and genuine offer' to Holyrood. Edinburgh's one matching commitment is £10 million for two defence technical colleges, and it is running its own local government reform programme in parallel."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F83",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "The meeting of the National Economic Council with the First Ministers of Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland, due in a couple of weeks, is the first point at which the offer can be shown to be taken up or not."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F14",
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13"
                ],
                "text": "Abroad, the Prime Minister raised the energy ceasefire with President Trump in New York, and Trump then announced it as reciprocal. But Ukraine has committed only to implement it once a start date is confirmed."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "N3"
                ],
                "text": "London is not waiting for that date. A sanctions package now covers over 90% of Russia's oil producing capacity, and a maritime services ban on Russian LNG is to be fully implemented. £10 million of a £45 million surface-to-air missile package is being sped up, and Ministers have been asked to draw up more packages. So the UK is squeezing Russian energy revenue at the same time as it backs a ceasefire on energy targets."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S8:F27",
                  "S8:F85",
                  "S4:F19"
                ],
                "text": "The next fixed date is the UK-EU summit in Brussels on 20 November. There the Prime Minister wants a new food and farming deal, which he pitched in his Scotland speech, after telling Berlin that Germany could join the Global Combat Air Programme."
              }
            ],
            "stories": []
          }
        }
      ],
